// Tests nested `previous` wrapping a `since` expression. The `since`
// operator requires the right arm to hold at EVERY time point between
// anchor and decision — including the decision point itself. Since the
// Alert at @30 is not a Heartbeat, bare `since` fails. Wrapping in
// `previous within` shifts evaluation to @20 (the prior time point),
// which does satisfy the chain.
//
// Trace: Login(@0) → HB(@10) → HB(@20) → Alert(@30)
// At @30 with `previous`: checks the since condition up to @20, where
// HB holds and has a previous HB at @10 → true.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Alert",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    previous within 2h (Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.server } since within 2h (Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat"::request{ input.server: context.input.server } && previous within 1h Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat"::request{ input.server: context.input.server }))
};
